@startuml
' The dependency rule inside one service binary (or the framework):
' adapters -> ports -> domain, and never the other way round.
' Rendered into docs/architecture/overview.md.

skinparam backgroundColor transparent
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam roundCorner 6

skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #7A7A7A
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #6E6E6E
  FontStyle bold
}

title Hexagonal layering — dependencies point inward only

package "Adapters — infra-aware" as adapters #FDF3E7 {
  rectangle "gRPC adapter\n(api/...)"                       as AGrpc
  rectangle "Consul adapter\n(registration + discovery)"    as AConsul
  rectangle "scaffold generator\n(cpp_tmpl.py)"             as AScaffold
  rectangle "FastAPI bridge\n(REST front)"                  as ABridge
  rectangle "Nomad subprocess manager"                      as ANomad
}

package "Ports — interfaces / protocols" as ports #EEF4FB {
  rectangle "service registry port"   as Pregistry
  rectangle "process lifecycle port"  as Plife
  rectangle "serialization port"      as Pserial
  rectangle "subprocess port"         as Pproc
}

package "Domain — zero-deps" as domain #EDF6ED {
  rectangle "Service business logic\nplain functions + value types\nno grpc / fastapi / consul / nomad / qt\nunit-testable in isolation" as D
}

adapters --> ports  : talks via
ports    --> domain : consumed by
domain   ..> adapters : **never** reaches up

@enduml
